README: Arduino Sketch Setup for Aimbot Configuration and Control

•••••••• ⚠️ Warning••••••••
This Arduino sketch is part of an educational project for studying input emulation and serial communication. It is not intended for cheating in online games. Use only in offline or test environments.

🧰 Compatibility
Works with Arduino boards that support USB mouse emulation: Leonardo, Micro, Due, Zero, etc.
Not compatible with boards that do not support native mouse emulation.

⚙️ Installation and Upload Instructions

	○ Open the Arduino IDE and create a new sketch.
	○ Paste the code into the editor.
	○ Select the board:
	○ Tools → Board → Arduino Leonardo (or your specific board).
	○ Select the port:
	○ Tools → Port → choose the COM port to which the Arduino board is connected (e.g., COM3, COM6).
	○ If the port is not visible, reinstall the drivers or check the USB cable.
	○ Click the Upload button (the right‑pointing arrow).
	○ Wait until the message “Done uploading” appears in the bottom panel.
