🔌 Connection and Configuration

Python Side (aimbot.py)
In the configuration/GUI of the Python script:

1)arduino_port: Set to the same COM port as in the Arduino IDE (e.g., COM3).
2)baud_rate: Must match the sketch setting: 115200.
3)input_mode: Set to arduino.

Example configuration snippet:




_____________________________
{
  "arduino_port": "COM3",
  "baud_rate": 115200,
  "input_mode": "arduino"
}
_____________________________


	✅ Verification Checklist
	
	○ Board is Leonardo/Micro/etc. (supports Mouse.h).
	○ The sketch compiles and uploads without errors.
	○ COM port in the Python script matches the one in the Arduino IDE.
	○ Baud rate is the same on both sides (115200).
	○ Python script is run as Administrator.
	○ Game is running in Borderless Windowed mode (to avoid capture/input issues).
	○ No other program is using the same COM port.

